Risk Quantification with FAIR and Monte Carlo
Objectives
By completing this lab, you will:

Set up an open-source FAIR risk quantification stack on Linux
Decompose a real risk scenario using FAIR taxonomy (LEF, LM, TC, Vuln, PLM/SLM)
Model uncertainty using Monte Carlo simulation with appropriate probability distributions
Generate and interpret Loss Exceedance Curves (LEC)
Produce an executive-ready quantitative risk report mapped to CGRC risk communication requirements
Prerequisites
Working knowledge of Python (functions, classes, numpy/pandas)
Understanding of FAIR taxonomy (Loss Event Frequency, Loss Magnitude, Threat Capability, Control Strength)
Familiarity with probability distributions (PERT, lognormal, triangular)
Basic Linux CLI competency
Conceptual grasp of CGRC risk assessment/reporting domains
