Conclusion
In this lab, you architected and implemented a full FAIR-based quantitative risk analysis pipeline on a single Linux machine using open-source tools. You decomposed a realistic third-party/cloud data breach scenario into FAIR taxonomy factors, designed and implemented probability distributions for uncertain inputs, built a vectorized Monte Carlo engine to compute Annualized Loss Exposure, and visualized results via a Loss Exceedance Curve. Finally, you translated statistical output into a board-ready report with actionable risk treatment recommendations — directly applicable to the CGRC domains of risk assessment, monitoring, and reporting, and to real-world enterprise risk management decision-making.
